      "writtenOn": "2024-02-26T09:37:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I updated the doc to say that \"A service is considered expired if any of its DNS record is expired\".\n\nFor Thread, I think the discovery proxy spec requires per-record expiration but I also think it\u0027s  a bit over complicated to return a per-record TTL given the fact that TTL will be capped to 10 seconds (which I think happens for the 99% real world use cases). Secondly, I think it\u0027s still useful to have a per-service level expiration for clients to know for how long they can safely refer to the info in the discovered NsdServiceInfo.\n\nSo I am keeping the API signature unchanged here. Let\u0027s look back at this if there are real discovery proxy issues with this.",
